The plate looks like a square dinner plate about 26 cm across, which in the image spans roughly 450 px, so about 17 px per cm. The scrambled eggs cover roughly 200 px by 240 px, or about 12 cm by 14 cm at the longest. That is a modest pile, perhaps 3-4 cm high at the center.

I estimate the volume at about 150-200 ml. Scrambled eggs are loose and airy, so the mass is about 120-150 g. Cooked scrambled eggs run about 150-200 kcal per 100 g once butter or oil is included. At around 140 g and 1.5 kcal/g, that comes to about 210 kcal.

